    <bpmn:process id="W_W4750" name="W4750. Rental Vehicle Preventive Maintenance, Safety Inspection &amp; Servicing Schedule" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Mileage interval; calendar interval; rental return (W4759); OBD fault code
Frequency: Per vehicle every ~5,000 km or 3 months + per-rental safety check
Volume: ~600–800 vehicles × ~4 services/yr ≈ ~2,400–3,200 services/yr + ~every-rental check
Owner: Rental Fleet Maintenance Lead / Fleet (VS-06)
Participants: Service workshop/parts (VS-31), Store Maintenance (VS-07.2), Telematics (W4749)
Source: workflow W4750 — Rental Vehicle Preventive Maintenance, Safety Inspection &amp; Servicing Schedule</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4750_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4750_Lane1" name="Fleet Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4750_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4750_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4750_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4750_Lane2" name="Store Maintenance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4750_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4750_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4750_Start4" name="Mileage interval; calendar interval; rental return (W4759); OBD fault code">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4750_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4750_Task5" name="Run the preventive-maintenance schedule per mileage/calendar: engine oil…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Run the preventive-maintenance schedule per mileage/calendar: engine oil, filters, brakes, tires (tread + pressure — critical for a loaded rental), battery, suspension, lights, belts, and the cargo-area/tie-down/tailgate check; trigger from telematics mileage (W4749)
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance / Service Workshop
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Maintenance Lead
Duration: Per service</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4750_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4750_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4750_Task6" name="between-rental safety check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Perform the between-rental safety check on every vehicle before re-release: tires/brakes/lights/steering, fire extinguisher/first-aid/jack/spare, cargo tie-downs, no fluid leaks, no dashboard warning; record the checklist and block re-release on any fail
Responsible (R): Store Maintenance / Rental Counter
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Maintenance Lead
Duration: Per rental</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4750_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4750_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4750_Task7" name="Manage defects found at return (W4759) or via OBD fault codes: triage, repair…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manage defects found at return (W4759) or via OBD fault codes: triage, repair vs ground, parts lead time (links VS-31), substitute-vehicle provisioning for customers with active reservations, and the downtime cost/impact on availability KPI
Responsible (R): Fleet Maintenance / Service Workshop
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Maintenance Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4750_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4750_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4750_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4750_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-94 (ensure rental fleet safety &amp; settlement integrity.) | - CTL-716: PM every 5,000 km / 3 mo; between-rental safety check before every re-release; defect-grounding enforced
Owner: Rental Fleet Maintenance Lead / Fleet (VS-06)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
